#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:127
msgid "Customize the Rendering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:129
msgid ""
"If you need more control over the rendering of the HTML, you can "
"implement a ``render()`` method. This method allows you to perform "
"additional logic and pass extra data the view, if needed. The "
"``render()`` method must return a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:131
msgid ""
"To take advantage of the full features of controlled Cells, you should "
"use ``$this->view()`` instead of the normal ``view()`` helper function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:136
msgid "Computed Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:138
msgid ""
"If you need to perform additional logic for one or more properties you "
"can use computed properties. These require setting the property to either"
" ``protected`` or ``private`` and implementing a public method whose name"
" consists of the property name surrounded by ``get`` and ``Property``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:146
msgid ""
"You can't set properties that are declared as private during cell "
"initialization. Calling ``getDataProperty()`` and ``getViewProperty()`` "
"methods are not available - they are used only for internal processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:151
msgid "Presentation Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:153
msgid ""
"Sometimes you need to perform additional logic for the view, but you "
"don't want to pass it as a parameter. You can implement a method that "
"will be called from within the cell's view itself. This can help the "
"readability of your views: You may have noticed that not only method "
"calls are allowed in the template: the entire Сell object with public "
"properties is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/view_cells.rst:162
msgid "Performing Setup Logic"
